 "content_notes": "Closed case: John Allen Muhammad was convicted in Virginia in 2003 and executed on 10 November 2009; Lee Boyd Malvo (17 at the time) was given life sentences, a Maryland resentencing ordered in 2022 has stalled and the Maryland Supreme Court refused his appeal in August 2026 (card: 'resentencing fights continue'). No shooting, weapon, victim, injury or crime scene is depicted: the toll is a typed card at a briefing; the Alabama beat is a storefront exterior at dusk with an evidence marker; the trunk is said only to have been 'modified'. Victims are not named; the memorial card says only 'the ten who died'. Muhammad and Malvo appear ONLY as anonymous rim-lit silhouettes (not likenesses, never photo recreations) and as dark shapes inside the car; none of their words, calls, notes or beliefs are quoted. The truck driver is a generic, unnamed figure; the officers are generic, with no insignia and no weapons. The sedan is a generic dark blue 1990s car with a BLANK plate; the rest stop, road, store and offices are generic drawings with no real name, number, sign or logo. Every card is our own typed graphic; no real police, court or FBI material is imitated. No dialogue is invented. Legal status verified 2026-10-13.",
